{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5","id":1531976,"title":"Ten Tips for using Hauglosk in W5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-04T13:50:52-08:00","id":1531976,"title":"Ten Tips for using Hauglosk in W5","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/03/ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/03/ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/03/ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/03/ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of the more controversial elements of Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th Edition is the introduction of the condition of Hauglosk. Hauglosk is effectively the opposite of Harano. While a Garou suffering Harano is someone who sinks into all consuming despair and depression from the futility of their struggles with the Wyrm, a Garou suffering Hauglosk throws themselves into the jaws of the Wyrm in hopes of clawing their way out from their stomach.<br /> <br /> A werewolf suffering from Hauglosk is someone who is infected by a form of fanatical zeal that effectively turns them into a Gaian fundamentalist terrorist. W:TA's corebook says it best (page 52): &quot;In a desperate fight against an overwhelming enemy, the ends justify the means. Everything is on the table. Victory at any cost. This is hauglosk, the conviction that your absolute moral certainty justifies everything you do.Hauglosk is a state of extreme righteousness. A Garou in a state of hauglosk believes that the cause is all, that their way is the only way.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given Gaia is dying, Hauglosk seems less like an overreaction and more like the proper attitude to the imminent end of everything. At least to some Garou. Even some long-time players question its utility as it seems like a mechanization of a roleplaying condition. Here are some thoughts on how I'm incorporating Hauglosk into W5.<br /> <br /> <b>1. Hauglosk is a choice</b><br /> <br /> Hauglosk should not be treated as the Dark Side of the Force or the One Ring of Power. It's more insidious than that but more a series of compromises and choices that a Garou proceeds to make before they gradually destroy everything worthwhile in them as an honorable warrior of Gaia. It is supernatural and a reflection of the Garou's rage and drive combined with their human minds but not so much that it is not identifiable as having a specific cause then effect. Storytellers attempting to use Hauglosk in their games shoudn't rely on the mechanics of it versus the storytelling beats of it. At what point does a Garou cease caring about the collateral damage in their quest to protect Gaia? At what point does culling humans seem right? What about those Garou who are traitors because they're not pulling their weight? Hauglosk is a state that comes in degrees but one that are all too easy to make rationalizations before.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Hauglosk is fundamentalist</b><br /> <br /> Hauglosk is religious fundamentalism, authoritarian militarism, and &quot;my way is only way&quot; blind unthinking fanaticism. Garou suffering for it believe their way is the only salvation for the world and everyone who believes otherwise is either evil or stupid. It can also manifest itself in multiple ways from the Gaian warrior who will do anything to save her to the Litany zealot who thinks any Gaia who refuses to follow ancient outdated interpretations is a blasphemer to the racial purist who has belief that only certain Garou families should survive.<br /> <br /> <b>3. Hauglosk is self-defeating</b><br /> <br /> A thing that STs dealing with Hauglosk should remember is the fact that it's a condition that will utimately provide easy answers but, ultimately, wrong ones. The Cult of Fenris turned against the entirety of the Garou Nation because no one would agree with their plan to launch a suicide attack on Malfeas. Now they are warring with their fellow Garou, which certainly is not helping the war against the Wyrm. A Hauglosk infected Silver Fang may decide the only way to save Gaia is to reaffirm their tribes' position of absolute leadership and force all the other tribes to acknowlege it. Another might think the Impergium needs a sequel despite how impossible and stupid said idea is. Hauglosk provides a sense of you having figured out THE SOLUTIONtm and everyone else is just too dumb to see it.<br /> <br /> <b>4. Hauglosk has always been there</b><br /> <br /> One interpretation of Hauglosk is the fact that it is a Garou condition that has been afflicting them since the Impergium and War of Rage but one that's never been wildly addressed among the Children of Luna. Zeal is a virtue among the Garou after all and blind unthinking fanaticism is something that religious cults (of which the Garou could be described as) often extoll rather than condemn. Recognizing it is a problem is, if not something new, something that the Garou are only now coming to terms with in the Modern Nights. However, that means the Garou have to go up against centuries, if not millennia, of institutional inertia.<br /> <br /> <b>5. Hauglosk is probably everywhere in the Garou Nation</b><br /> <br /> The Get of Fenris falling to Hauglosk is something that has massively damaged the Garou's ability to fight as well as their unity as a whole. Blaming it on Hauglosk is almost a cop out because that let's all of the other tribes off the hook. Except, what if they aren't off the hook at all? What if Hauglosk is rampant throughout the entirety of the Garou Nation? What if it has already taken one or more of them (*cough* Red Talons *cough)?<br /> <br /> What if the only reason anyone noticed the Cult suffering from it was because they chose to turn against their fellows? What if most sufferers of Hauglosk are just on a downward spiral that will end with their &quot;heroic&quot; deaths and becoming examples for others? The Stargazers left the Garou Nation for a reason. Maybe it was because they felt their fellows couldn't be helped.<br /> <br /> <b>6. Can Hauglosk be cured?</b><br /> <br /> There's no system for recovery from Hauglosk but that doesn't necessarily mean that it is incurable in-universe (or maybe it is--ST's perogitive). However, if you are going to allow it to be cured then there's no easy fix. Cult deprogramming is a debunked practice for good reason. However, people do escape from fudnamentalist views and extremist ideologies. It is just a long and difficult process. Storyteller's should determine whether it's possible to cure Hauglosk with either rites, roleplaying, or cleansing by spirits. However, it should probably be done by convincing a Garou to try to fix themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>7. Hauglosk should be tempting</b><br /> <br /> Despite Hauglosk being best used as a metaphor for fanaticism and single-minded obsession, it should be something that the Storyteller willingly inserts as a temptation for player characters. Think of it as the voice of the Shadow in Wraith: The Oblivion or the Devil on the shoulder. The ST should not necessarily be overt about it but present opportunities to increase Hauglosk through single-minded obsessive zeal. The chance to win over a clan by gutting a Child of Gaia who advocates for a more peaceful solution or mentioning how disgusting a Kin who has abandoned the war for Gaia to live a &quot;normal&quot; life is.<br /> <br /> <b>8. The downward spiral is not necessarily to be avoided</b><br /> <br /> This is something that should be suggested to a player before a ST starts the idea but the roleplaying of a character succumbing to their worst impulses isn't necessarily a bad arc to explore at one's table. If a player is game, his character gradually becoming more radicalized and fanatical in the service of Gaia then it could eb a very interesting plot arc. Do they pull out of their nosedive in time or abandon themselves wholly to madness?<br /> <br /> <b>9. Identifying Hauglosk should not be easy</b><br /> <br /> Hauglosk is insidious and powerful because it is something that is entirely in line with a strict reading of Garou values. Its users want to save Gaia, its users want to fight the Wyrm, and its users argue that the situation is desperate--which is all correct. They do not so much hide behind tradition as believe that it is the failure of the Garou to do ENOUGH that has caused them to lose the Apocalypse rather than the idea they have gone too far. Many Garou agree with this sentiment even if they are not in agreement over what &quot;enough&quot; would look like. What is the difference between a Red Talon who wants to cull ninety-percent of all humans and one who has been consumed by their inner rage? Is there? And is the Garou Nation turning a blind eye to how deep the rot is?<br /> <br /> <b>10. Purging Hauglosk may require extreme measures</b><br /> <br /> One of the greatest victories the Garou achieved of the 21st century was the purging of Sword of Heimdall. It was an act that eliminated some of the worst of their kind and was done by the Get to try to redeem themselves. Sadly, it did not work. The Garou have been reforming themselves for the past two decades but that reform did not come fast enough for the Get and may not come fast enough for the Garou Nation to be saved. Ironically, an extreme solution may be the only way to end the extremism that would have the Garou all commit collective suicide by embracing worthless acts of fanaticism over seeking more cunning solutions. Is the man who suggests they slay all the Red Talons' favoring genocide insane, Hauglosk ridden, or correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":7},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T16:45:58-08:00","id":1531983,"title":"","content":"Lot of downvotes, I wonder what people don't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:26:00-08:00","id":1532010,"title":"","content":"Being obliged to confront the notion that something from 5th Edition WEREWOLF can actually be useful, rather than dismissed to the Realm of Ghosts &amp; Shadows?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:34:33-08:00","id":1532012,"title":"","content":"One notion I think needs to be knocked on the head is the idea of a \u2018Cure\u2019 for Hauglosk: this strikes me as a condition that can be treated and managed, but not as something you can reasonably expect to get rid of - like Harano, it\u2019s an intrinsic hazard of the Garou psyche and possibly even inherent to the nature of the People.<br /> <br /> After all, Rage is like Fire - an elemental force that represents an invaluable tool, a dangerous servant and a poor master. It is, in fact, intrinsic to the Garou condition to the point where they lose their most fundamental ability without it, so one cannot reasonably hope to do without it.<br /> <br /> A Garou can, however, work to use it well and not simply throw themselves into the downward spiral of explosives launched in a carpet bombing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:35:14-08:00","id":1532013,"title":"","content":"By the way, my compliments on a fine article!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T07:58:29-08:00","id":1532028,"title":"","content":"I didn't down vote you but I can break down where I disagree with your analysis of the text in a few spots.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is tied to fanaticism in only really one small section of W5. All the others it is clearly tied to fascism specifically. This is made apparently clear in both the Cult of Fenris write up and the Fascism in Play sections of the books.<br /> <br /> With that in mind I think your point 7 can rub people the wrong way if you don't address or remove that aspect of Hauglosk (which is fairly engrained in W5's DNA imo). <br /> <br /> To point 6, once again the text hints at it being uncurable. Especially since players lose their characters once the tracker has been filled RAW. In addition, the BSDs can be cured with remarkable ease. All it takes is 1 maxed out loresheet and a roll after a period of isolation with the BSD. Why is the Wyrm tribe easier to cure than Gaian fanaticism? I would, if I was ever inclined to run W5 again, snag the concept that was hinted at in the Sambrano writings on the HE tribes. Where it is an over exaggeration of each tribe's ideals for a period of time or curable as the meter goes up.<br /> <br /> To point 4. The Garou are part human. Humans do atrocities all the time. They don't need a supernatural condition to do it. IMO the lore is from the POV of the Garou who try to make excuses for the choices they make. I think tying it to a supernatural condition is a mistake.<br /> <br /> I think, fundamentally, Hauglosk misses the point of what Werewolf should be. In that violence is necessary sometimes but it isn't the only tool that's necessary. The Garou have to build after they destroy, they have to destroy the right things, etc. With Hauglosk it's the same problem I had with the last season of Game of Thrones &quot;Oops, Dany went crazy because she believed in ending slavery too much&quot; which just doesn't work and kind of missed the point of the source material. Something that W5 seems to do frequently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:52:48-08:00","id":1532036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532010#post1532010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being obliged to confront the notion that something from 5th Edition WEREWOLF can actually be useful, rather than dismissed to the Realm of Ghosts &amp; Shadows?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Useful for what? Making your players want to quit the game? Serving as a blueprint for Anti-Golconda? Acting as a herald of reasons not to stick around to see how the design team handles M5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:54:45-08:00","id":1532037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532028#post1532028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, fundamentally, Hauglosk misses the point of what Werewolf should be. In that violence is necessary sometimes but it isn't the only tool that's necessary. The Garou have to build after they destroy, they have to destroy the right things, etc. With Hauglosk it's the same problem I had with the last season of Game of Thrones &quot;Oops, Dany went crazy because she believed in ending slavery too much&quot; which just doesn't work and kind of missed the point of the source material. Something that W5 seems to do frequently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly my only point of contention is that Martin absolutely is setting up Danny to fail because he's made taking over the Slavers Bay folk and ending slavery analogous to the Occupation in Iraq.<br /> <br /> Which as a guy born in the South who wishes the North had gone farther in rooting out slaver culture, is RIDICULOUS.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:55:36-08:00","id":1532038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532036#post1532036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Useful for what? Making your players want to quit the game? Serving as a blueprint for Anti-Golconda? Acting as a herald of reasons not to stick around to see how the design team handles M5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to hear your perspective on the article and what you agreed and disagreed with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:00:54-08:00","id":1532040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532037#post1532037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oddly my only point of contention is that Martin absolutely is setting up Danny to fail because he's made taking over the Slavers Bay folk and ending slavery analogous to the Occupation in Iraq.<br /> <br /> Which as a guy born in the South who wishes the North had gone farther in rooting out slaver culture, is RIDICULOUS.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll only be off topic here briefly. I think he set her up to fail because she failed to do reconstruction. She freed them and then didn't do anything to improve their living conditions. She didn't rebuild anything after destroying it. Similar to my point of the Garou <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:11:34-08:00","id":1532041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532040#post1532040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll only be off topic here briefly. I think he set her up to fail because she failed to do reconstruction. She freed them and then didn't do anything to improve their living conditions. She didn't rebuild anything after destroying it. Similar to my point of the Garou <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tying it back to the Garou, I'd argue differently. She didn't go FURTHER in her destruction of the old slaver families. You gotta go full Seventh Generation and rip em out root and stem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:24:59-08:00","id":1532042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A Bunch of Gamers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532028#post1532028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't down vote you but I can break down where I disagree with your analysis of the text in a few spots.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is tied to fanaticism in only really one small section of W5. All the others it is clearly tied to fascism specifically. This is made apparently clear in both the Cult of Fenris write up and the Fascism in Play sections of the books.<br /> <br /> With that in mind I think your point 7 can rub people the wrong way if you don't address or remove that aspect of Hauglosk (which is fairly engrained in W5's DNA imo).<br /> <br /> To point 6, once again the text hints at it being uncurable. Especially since players lose their characters once the tracker has been filled RAW. In addition, the BSDs can be cured with remarkable ease. All it takes is 1 maxed out loresheet and a roll after a period of isolation with the BSD. Why is the Wyrm tribe easier to cure than Gaian fanaticism? I would, if I was ever inclined to run W5 again, snag the concept that was hinted at in the Sambrano writings on the HE tribes. Where it is an over exaggeration of each tribe's ideals for a period of time or curable as the meter goes up.<br /> <br /> To point 4. The Garou are part human. Humans do atrocities all the time. They don't need a supernatural condition to do it. IMO the lore is from the POV of the Garou who try to make excuses for the choices they make. I think tying it to a supernatural condition is a mistake.<br /> <br /> I think, fundamentally, Hauglosk misses the point of what Werewolf should be. In that violence is necessary sometimes but it isn't the only tool that's necessary. The Garou have to build after they destroy, they have to destroy the right things, etc. With Hauglosk it's the same problem I had with the last season of Game of Thrones &quot;Oops, Dany went crazy because she believed in ending slavery too much&quot; which just doesn't work and kind of missed the point of the source material. Something that W5 seems to do frequently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing my mind to address a few things:<br /> <br /> 1. Fascism is certainly the bugaboo of W5 and certainly a problem in the real world. However, the fact is that it's not really a great fit for the Garou as a whole. Especially since it's fairly easy to draw a comparison between religious fundamentalism (which can go with fascism as we see in America and Franco's Spain) and the Garou Nation. The problem is that they cleaned up the Litany of some of its more ridiculous tenats like &quot;Garou shall not mate with Garou&quot; so there's less overtly objectionable and less ridiculous tenats to rebel against.<br /> <br /> 2. This point reminds me of INGLORIOUS BASTERDS where one of the people I most respect in the world hated the fact that I refused to engage with the film's message that the protagonists were becoming every bit as awful as the Nazis they fought by becoming monsters to fight fascists. My response is, &quot;Yeah, but they're killing Nazis so....I'm okay with it.&quot; Hauglosk seems like a very easy place to explore the, &quot;He who gazes in the abyss too long finds it gazing right back.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, which is why this is a fan document asking the ST to decide whether it's curable or not. That is something that is left to the table to do so. It doesn't say it's NOT incurable, though. It doesn't give a system for it, though. Which is the same as V5 and Humanity yet absolutely regaining Humanity is a thing in the setting.<br /> <br /> 4. Humans also suffer depression but Harano is a system that has been there since W1. It's just an extrapolation for reflecting a very Garou specific issue, IMHO. Yes, it might be supernatural PTSD but it's still a metaphor for RL PTSD. Just the same as Hauglosk is supernatural radicalization of ideology but still just a metaphor for RL radicalization.<br /> <br /> 5. I don't think Hauglosk &quot;misses the point&quot; of WTA but simply adds a new dimension to the struggle of saying, &quot;So, you think that saving Gaia at all costs is worth it? Well, what does that REALLY look like?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that I'm not disagreeing with any of your criticisms, I'm just saying discussing them makes for a more enriching WTA experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:45:33-08:00","id":1532044,"title":"","content":"The problem is that the W5 corebook has linked both Harano and Hauglosk to real-world-concepts. So the first issue is that with these connections in play, the way these two conditions have to be treated has to be way more nuanced. Harano is linked to depression which is real-world mental-health-condition. And Hauglosk is linked to becoming a fascist/Nazi in the W5 corebook. Neither of these are light topics to bring to a gaming-table. Not taking that seriously and how players could potentially react to those topics is just a sign of being a bad GM/Storyteller. Therefore, I think another point that needs to be added to the list as a tip is that you absolutely need to discuss the definitions and implications of these two things with the players in a session zero. And then you need to adjust the concepts to what the players think about them.<br /> <br /> And then there's the Age of Apocalypse. Any extremism when it comes to fighting the enemy gets lessened when you raise the stakes to &quot;The end of the world is close, <i>very </i>close.&quot;. You're really stacking the deck for any consequentialist moral argument by having that be part of the setting. Any utilitarian analysis would be 100% on the side of the Cult of Fenris in that environment and consider them to be the morally good side in the setting when the alternative is just hiding in a caern. So, another thing I would add (which isn't part of the W5 corebook) is to make clear that there's a way to prevent the Apocalypse that doesn't involve becoming ecofascists that pursue a scorched earth campaign against the Wyrm and everything that's directly or indirectly linked to it. Hauglosk can only be a bad solution to the problem when there's another good solution to the problem. Just saying Hauglosk is bad isn't good enough in the context of W5. Do I let the forces win who are close to ending the world or do I uphold my personal virtues? That isn't an interesting trolley-problem. Is my own morality more important than saving the world? There's nothing interesting about that - unless you want to make it a tragedy. But you need player-buy-in first for that. If you don't have that, Hauglosk is a waste of time. Without a better alternative, Hauglosk is acceptable behavior in the Age of Apocalypse. If anything, it would contribute to the concept of the Age of Apocalypse since order will break down, of course, as the world gets closer to its death. That's a huge problem with the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T09:55:38-08:00","id":1532046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532044#post1532044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the W5 corebook has linked both Harano and Hauglosk to real-world-concepts. So the first issue is that with these connections in play, the way these two conditions have to be treated has to be way more nuanced. Harano is linked to depression which is real-world mental-health-condition. And Hauglosk is linked to becoming a fascist/Nazi in the W5 corebook. Neither of these are light topics to bring to a gaming-table. Not taking that seriously and how players could potentially react to those topics is just a sign of being a bad GM/Storyteller. Therefore, I think another point that needs to be added to the list as a tip is that you absolutely need to discuss the definitions and implications of these two things with the players in a session zero. And then you need to adjust the concepts to what the players think about them.<br /> <br /> And then there's the Age of Apocalypse. Any extremism when it comes to fighting the enemy gets lessened when you raise the stakes to &quot;The end of the world is close, <i>very </i>close.&quot;. You're really stacking the deck for any consequentialist moral argument by having that be part of the setting. Any utilitarian analysis would be 100% on the side of the Cult of Fenris in that environment and consider them to be the morally good side in the setting when the alternative is just hiding in a caern. So, another thing I would add (which isn't part of the W5 corebook) is to make clear that there's a way to prevent the Apocalypse that doesn't involve becoming ecofascists that pursue a scorched earth campaign against the Wyrm and everything that's directly or indirectly linked to it. Hauglosk can only be a bad solution to the problem when there's another good solution to the problem. Just saying Hauglosk is bad isn't good enough in the context of W5. Do I let the forces win who are close to ending the world or do I uphold my personal virtues? That isn't an interesting trolley-problem. Is my own morality more important than saving the world? There's nothing interesting about that - unless you want to make it a tragedy. But you need player-buy-in first for that. If you don't have that, Hauglosk is a waste of time. Without a better alternative, Hauglosk is acceptable behavior in the Age of Apocalypse. If anything, it would contribute to the concept of the Age of Apocalypse since order will break down, of course, as the world gets closer to its death. That's a huge problem with the concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that I thought would get more attention, specifically Point 3.<br /> <br /> One of the things that I often discussed in my political science classes was the absolute importance of dismissing the &quot;Nazis were repressive but efficient myth.&quot; I didn't understand why this was important because whether or not fascism &quot;worked&quot; didn't seem remotely important because it was so monstrous ethically. Except that is the inherent argument of fascism that, &quot;ethics don't matter versus your goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> To keep it W:TA the simple fact is the Cult of Fenris has done nothing but massively make the situation for the Garou Nation and Gaia worse. They're having a Civil War when the barbarians at the gate and all hands need to be on deck. I don't think W5 was very well written and OPP would have done a 1000% better explaining it but the irony is the best thing the Garou nation could do is kill every single person advocating these &quot;at all costs&quot; people.<br /> <br /> Because they're idiots and their solutions <i>don't work</i>, which is a real problem in the Modern day with fascist. Global warming, environmentalism, and worse are going to kill us all--and the fascists are absolutely not going to make it better.<br /> <br /> But people go to it because they offer the appearance of a solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T10:24:12-08:00","id":1532048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532046#post1532046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is something that I thought would get more attention, specifically Point 3.<br /> <br /> One of the things that I often discussed in my political science classes was the absolute importance of dismissing the &quot;Nazis were repressive but efficient myth.&quot; I didn't understand why this was important because whether or not fascism &quot;worked&quot; didn't seem remotely important because it was so monstrous ethically. Except that is the inherent argument of fascism that, &quot;ethics don't matter versus your goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> To keep it W:TA the simple fact is the Cult of Fenris has done nothing but massively make the situation for the Garou Nation and Gaia worse. They're having a Civil War when the barbarians at the gate and all hands need to be on deck. I don't think W5 was very well written and OPP would have done a 1000% better explaining it but the irony is the best thing the Garou nation could do is kill every single person advocating these &quot;at all costs&quot; people.<br /> <br /> Because they're idiots and their solutions <i>don't work</i>, which is a real problem in the Modern day with fascist. Global warming, environmentalism, and worse are going to kill us all--and the fascists are absolutely not going to make it better.<br /> <br /> But people go to it because they offer the appearance of a solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta be honest. Sometimes this aspect weirds me out about W5. We know these fascist movements thrive on conspiracy-theories... elders of zion, great reset, QAnon... somehow they always convince themselves it's them against these dark forces that secretly control the world. And then you have the Cult of Fenris here who are fanatical warriors and who are linked to fascism/Nazis - but they're fighting to prevent the actual end of the world. Not these imagined conspiracy-theories as in the real world but instead, you have a fascistic movement fighting to prevent the end of the world (which is an actual thing in the setting).<br /> <br /> Personally, what I think would be more fitting for the Cult of Fenris as fascistic movement would be something like if Crinos-born Garou were still a thing... they convincing themselves that Gaia had withdrawn her favor from the Garou because she's gainst Crinos-born Garou and so if the Fenrir were to kill every single Crinos-born on the planet, everything would be fine. You know, just this wild assumption/conspiracy-theory. I think that's more for the depiction of the Cult, I guess, but that's the vibe Hauglosk needs to invoke. The W5 corebook should've mentioned the Cult's &quot;grand plan&quot; to prevent the Apocalypse and it should've been an intentionally stupid one, just this list of wild ideas that supposedly &quot;will fix everything&quot;. It wouldn't detract from the portrayal but make clear what's being invoked and why joining the Cult of Fenris isn't a solution.<br /> <br /> And then there's still the issue that I think this is a tough sell to players that their PCs are on the track to behaving like that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T11:32:54-08:00","id":1532049,"title":"","content":"Honestly as someone whose been fighting Nazis both on the street and online for a few decades now I just can't with W5s deeply centrist take on the entire thing ( Putting aside the loud pro-W5 voices who are incredibly quick to call Legacy fans Nazi sympathisers and get zero pushback for doing so in most WoD spaces online.).<br /> <br /> Fascists recruit by appealing to a perceived loss of power and suggesting simplistic solutions by generating scapegoats and othering to provide targets for venting frustrations. Today the vast majority of fascist recruitment lies in cults of celebrity linked to misogyny and other forms of bigotry it most certainly does not involve magical Clockwork Orange displays and psychological damage caused by violation of arbitrary rules of reality imposed from outside of the perception of fictional individuals.<br /> <br /> The idea that the CoF is in the wrong is deeply hurt by the depictions so far of every single non-Cult Garou doing less than nothing which gives the impression that taking any sort of direct action is being proscribed as equivalent to fanaticism. <br /> <br /> The CoF depictions need to decide what the Cult is....are they fanatics? Fanticism does not automatically lead to Fundamentalism and/or Fascism. And the same is true in all other directions. I think the writing for them suffers greatly because it has to work back from the directive that ' The Cult of Fenris' are Facist without doing anything to earn that organically so the entire thing feels kludged together with little meat on its bones.<br /> <br /> But what do i know.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T12:28:34-08:00","id":1532051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532042#post1532042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changing my mind to address a few things:<br /> <br /> 1. Fascism is certainly the bugaboo of W5 and certainly a problem in the real world. However, the fact is that it's not really a great fit for the Garou as a whole. Especially since it's fairly easy to draw a comparison between religious fundamentalism (which can go with fascism as we see in America and Franco's Spain) and the Garou Nation. The problem is that they cleaned up the Litany of some of its more ridiculous tenats like &quot;Garou shall not mate with Garou&quot; so there's less overtly objectionable and less ridiculous tenats to rebel against.<br /> <br /> 2. This point reminds me of INGLORIOUS BASTERDS where one of the people I most respect in the world hated the fact that I refused to engage with the film's message that the protagonists were becoming every bit as awful as the Nazis they fought by becoming monsters to fight fascists. My response is, &quot;Yeah, but they're killing Nazis so....I'm okay with it.&quot; Hauglosk seems like a very easy place to explore the, &quot;He who gazes in the abyss too long finds it gazing right back.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, which is why this is a fan document asking the ST to decide whether it's curable or not. That is something that is left to the table to do so. It doesn't say it's NOT incurable, though. It doesn't give a system for it, though. Which is the same as V5 and Humanity yet absolutely regaining Humanity is a thing in the setting.<br /> <br /> 4. Humans also suffer depression but Harano is a system that has been there since W1. It's just an extrapolation for reflecting a very Garou specific issue, IMHO. Yes, it might be supernatural PTSD but it's still a metaphor for RL PTSD. Just the same as Hauglosk is supernatural radicalization of ideology but still just a metaphor for RL radicalization.<br /> <br /> 5. I don't think Hauglosk &quot;misses the point&quot; of WTA but simply adds a new dimension to the struggle of saying, &quot;So, you think that saving Gaia at all costs is worth it? Well, what does that REALLY look like?&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is to say that I'm not disagreeing with any of your criticisms, I'm just saying discussing them makes for a more enriching WTA experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think point 1 and 2 are a matter of taste and differing interpretations of the text of the game. So I just disagree but I don't think any points will shift the conversation.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes and no. The book gives conflicting account. Pg 141 &quot;Hauglosk is also a long-term ongoing state, and <b>many Garou</b> never come out of it.&quot; and on the same page: &quot;If the tracker ever becomes filled, the werewolf has succumbed to hauglosk, becoming an <b>unredeemable </b>fanatic and a Storyteller character.&quot; Bold to highlight conflicting ideas.<br /> <br /> 4. I think the difference here is Harano has always been poorly defined in the rules and didn't have to be directly dealt with by the players if they didn't want to. In addition, Harano was written in Legacy as structural failures leading to supernatural despair VS Hauglosk in W5, which is written as supernatural fanaticism/fascism creates structural problems. Which is why I don't think the comparison is quite one to one. And kind of the core of why it rubs me the wrong way.<br /> <br /> 5. I think this has existed since the beginning and I think Hauglosk detracts. The reason is because it increases by either refreshing a resource or violating a chronicle tenant. One example in the book of chronicle tenants shows how this mechanic fails to support your thesis of adding a new dimension to play. Under the Apocalypse Radicalism example of chronicle tenants (pg 200) we see the following tenants:<br /> Do not cling to the old ways<br /> Never kill an outsider<br /> Vengeance must be served<br /> So RAW, if you gain information and another perspective where vengeance isn't the best option you become more fanatical? That seems like poor planning on the game's part. Or finding out some of the old or traditional ways are a good way of doing something and modernize other things makes you more willing to throw them out in the future? I'd argue it removes nuance by turning these deeper questions into an enforced mechanic.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28181-a-bunch-of-gamers","name":"A Bunch of Gamers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28181_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T12:57:02-08:00","id":1532052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532038#post1532038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd love to hear your perspective on the article and what you agreed and disagreed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're attempting to salvage the creative lead's desire to make feeling bad about being Garou compulsory; the desire to make the Fenrir entirely into the Swords of Heimdall, expanded from that noisome attempt to undo continuity until <b>all</b> the Garou are now inevitably either swallowed up by sorrow and die of self-neglect or suicide, or become like the Swords in mind if not in membership. It definitly feels like raw WoD game partisanship from the 90s, the construction of someone whose primary goal, after taking care of all the people who were playing Vampire the &quot;wrong&quot; way, was to stick it sideways to the people who liked the other games.<br /> <br /> I'd much rather continue being wrong and bad and having wrongbad fun according to the guy at the top who thought this was a good idea, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T13:40:35-08:00","id":1532053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532048#post1532048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gotta be honest. Sometimes this aspect weirds me out about W5. We know these fascist movements thrive on conspiracy-theories... elders of zion, great reset, QAnon... somehow they always convince themselves it's them against these dark forces that secretly control the world. And then you have the Cult of Fenris here who are fanatical warriors and who are linked to fascism/Nazis - <b>but they're fighting to prevent the actual end of the world.</b> Not these imagined conspiracy-theories as in the real world but instead, you have a fascistic movement fighting to prevent the end of the world (which is an actual thing in the setting).<br /> <br /> Personally, what I think would be more fitting for the Cult of Fenris as fascistic movement would be something like if Crinos-born Garou were still a thing... they convincing themselves that Gaia had withdrawn her favor from the Garou because she's gainst Crinos-born Garou and so if the Fenrir were to kill every single Crinos-born on the planet, everything would be fine. You know, just this wild assumption/conspiracy-theory. I think that's more for the depiction of the Cult, I guess, but that's the vibe Hauglosk needs to invoke. The W5 corebook should've mentioned the Cult's &quot;grand plan&quot; to prevent the Apocalypse and it should've been an intentionally stupid one, just this list of wild ideas that supposedly &quot;will fix everything&quot;. It wouldn't detract from the portrayal but make clear what's being invoked and why joining the Cult of Fenris isn't a solution.<br /> <br /> And then there's still the issue that I think this is a tough sell to players that their PCs are on the track to behaving like that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"715\" height=\"349\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I don't disagree with most of your post and think the Cult of Fenris loses some obvious baddie points by the fact the Crinosborn no longer exist. However, one of the things that I brought up with the &quot;Hauglosk is self-defeating&quot; point is the fact that the Cult of Fenris' primary goal right now is fighting other Garou. Fans complaining about the Get of Fenris/Cult of Fenris being all determined to go save Gaia miss that they're going after their fellow warriors to save Gaia. It's the equivalent of saying that the person who needs to be taken down in order to get Congress to finally pass the Green New Deal is AOC or Biden.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris aren't going after Pentex with a renewed fury, they're trying to take everyone else's caerns and magic items. Because ideological purity is more important than actually accomplishing their stated goal.<br /> <br /> I mean, we HAVE an example of a tribe who didn't think the Garou Nation was going to do anything good and left peacefully. It was the Stargazers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-05-2024, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T13:43:30-08:00","id":1532054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532049#post1532049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly as someone whose been fighting Nazis both on the street and online for a few decades now I just can't with W5s deeply centrist take on the entire thing ( Putting aside the loud pro-W5 voices who are incredibly quick to call Legacy fans Nazi sympathisers and get zero pushback for doing so in most WoD spaces online.).<br /> <br /> Fascists recruit by appealing to a perceived loss of power and suggesting simplistic solutions by generating scapegoats and othering to provide targets for venting frustrations. Today the vast majority of fascist recruitment lies in cults of celebrity linked to misogyny and other forms of bigotry it most certainly does not involve magical Clockwork Orange displays and psychological damage caused by violation of arbitrary rules of reality imposed from outside of the perception of fictional individuals.<br /> <br /> <b>The idea that the CoF is in the wrong is deeply hurt by the depictions so far of every single non-Cult Garou doing less than nothing which gives the impression that taking any sort of direct action is being proscribed as equivalent to fanaticism.</b><br /> <br /> The CoF depictions need to decide what the Cult is....are they fanatics? Fanticism does not automatically lead to Fundamentalism and/or Fascism. And the same is true in all other directions. I think the writing for them suffers greatly because it has to work back from the directive that ' The Cult of Fenris' are Facist without doing anything to earn that organically so the entire thing feels kludged together with little meat on its bones.<br /> <br /> But what do i know.....</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's the impression but it's not the way it's written or intended since the Garou Renown system and Gifts mean that you absolutely have to be doing SOMETHING or you don't get any power whatsoever.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Cult-Garou are doing something. They're killing other Garou for perceived not doing enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T13:45:37-08:00","id":1532055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532048#post1532048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gotta be honest. Sometimes this aspect weirds me out about W5. We know these fascist movements thrive on conspiracy-theories... elders of zion, great reset, QAnon... somehow they always convince themselves it's them against these dark forces that secretly control the world. And then you have the Cult of Fenris here who are fanatical warriors and who are linked to fascism/Nazis - <b>but they're fighting to prevent the actual end of the world.</b> Not these imagined conspiracy-theories as in the real world but instead, you have a fascistic movement fighting to prevent the end of the world (which is an actual thing in the setting).<br /> <br /> Personally, what I think would be more fitting for the Cult of Fenris as fascistic movement would be something like if Crinos-born Garou were still a thing... they convincing themselves that Gaia had withdrawn her favor from the Garou because she's gainst Crinos-born Garou and so if the Fenrir were to kill every single Crinos-born on the planet, everything would be fine. You know, just this wild assumption/conspiracy-theory. I think that's more for the depiction of the Cult, I guess, but that's the vibe Hauglosk needs to invoke. The W5 corebook should've mentioned the Cult's &quot;grand plan&quot; to prevent the Apocalypse and it should've been an intentionally stupid one, just this list of wild ideas that supposedly &quot;will fix everything&quot;. It wouldn't detract from the portrayal but make clear what's being invoked and why joining the Cult of Fenris isn't a solution.<br /> <br /> And then there's still the issue that I think this is a tough sell to players that their PCs are on the track to behaving like that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><img width=\"715\" height=\"349\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgflip.com/8dmns5.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I don't disagree with most of your post and think the Cult of Fenris loses some obvious baddie points by the fact the Crinosborn no longer exist. However, one of the things that I brought up with the &quot;Hauglosk is self-defeating&quot; point is the fact that the Cult of Fenris' primary goal right now is fighting other Garou. Fans complaining about the Get of Fenris/Cult of Fenris being all determined to go save Gaia miss that they're going after their fellow warriors to save Gaia. It's the equivalent of saying that the person who needs to be taken down in order to get Congress to finally pass the Green New Deal is AOC or Biden.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris aren't going after Pentex with a renewed fury, they're trying to take everyone else's caerns and magic items. Because ideological purity is more important than actually accomplishing their stated goal.<br /> <br /> I mean, we HAVE an example of a tribe who didn't think the Garou Nation was going to do anything good and left peacefully. It was the Stargazers.<br /> <br /> But then again, I think the idea that the Cult of Fenris being a bunch of idiots making the problem worse in the name of making it better is central to their handling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T13:59:48-08:00","id":1532058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532055#post1532055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree with most of your post and think the Cult of Fenris loses some obvious baddie points by the fact the Crinosborn no longer exist. However, one of the things that I brought up with the &quot;Hauglosk is self-defeating&quot; point is the fact that the Cult of Fenris' primary goal right now is fighting other Garou. Fans complaining about the Get of Fenris/Cult of Fenris being all determined to go save Gaia miss that they're going after their fellow warriors to save Gaia. It's the equivalent of saying that the person who needs to be taken down in order to get Congress to finally pass the Green New Deal is AOC or Biden.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Fenris aren't going after Pentex with a renewed fury, they're trying to take everyone else's caerns and magic items. Because ideological purity is more important than actually accomplishing their stated goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's objectively wrong. As part of their fanaticism and fascism, the Cult will attack other Garou but that isn't their main-goal and the W5 corebook is pretty clear on this (pg 279): &quot;What Do They Want: The Cult of Fenris wants to fight the Wyrm, but its Garou see the presence of the Wyrm in all things. As a result, they effectively seek their own version of Valhalla: Gaia is under a doom, and all anyone can do is fight while infinitely screaming her name until they fall\u2026 and then, ideally, fight on as a magnificent spirit limned in a halo of one\u2019s own gloriously pure opposition to the Wyrm. Being part of the Cult means never admitting you\u2019ve lost.&quot; The primary goal of the Cult is to fight the Wyrm. And Deepest of Wounds was about the Cult organizing a raiding-party that went out, leaving behind their dead caern to fight the forces of the Wyrm. The issue with the Cult is that they go too far in their pursuit of the Wyrm's forces and that they're ruthless in how they treat any perceived obstacles to their brutal methods (including other Gaian Garou). But <i>the Cult's main-goal is to attack the Wyrm</i> and its minions. That's how the corebook describes it and how it has been described in Deepest of Wounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T14:03:53-08:00","id":1532059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532058#post1532058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's objectively wrong. As part of their fanaticism and fascism, the Cult will attack other Garou but that isn't their main-goal and the W5 corebook is pretty clear on this (pg 279): &quot;What Do They Want: The Cult of Fenris wants to fight the Wyrm, but its Garou see the presence of the Wyrm in all things. As a result, they effectively seek their own version of Valhalla: Gaia is under a doom, and all anyone can do is fight while infinitely screaming her name until they fall\u2026 and then, ideally, fight on as a magnificent spirit limned in a halo of one\u2019s own gloriously pure opposition to the Wyrm. Being part of the Cult means never admitting you\u2019ve lost.&quot; The primary goal of the Cult is to fight the Wyrm. And Deepest of Wounds was about the Cult organizing a raiding-party that went out, leaving behind their dead caern to fight the forces of the Wyrm. The issue with the Cult is that they go too far in their pursuit of the Wyrm's forces and that they're ruthless in how they treat any perceived obstacles to their brutal methods (including other Gaian Garou). But <i>the Cult's main-goal is to attack the Wyrm</i> and its minions. That's how the corebook describes it and how it has been described in Deepest of Wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, you can read it as that.<br /> <br /> But it also says that everything has the Wyrm to them, especially other Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T14:17:30-08:00","id":1532060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532059#post1532059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, yes, you can read it as that.<br /> <br /> But it also says that everything has the Wyrm to them, especially other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>sigh<br /> <br /> It says &quot;What do they want: The Cult of Fenris wants to fight the Wyrm, but its Garou see the presence of the Wyrm in all things.&quot; There's no &quot;especially other Garou&quot; here. It's pretty straightforward. Look, I like your version more but the thing is: It's not the official version that's in the corebook. The corebook disagrees with you on this. And Deepest of Wounds follows that. When the Fenrir-caern dies in the setup of that adventure, they start a raiding-party to venture out and go after the Wyrm. They don't turn on the other Garou in their vicinity, they go out and look for Wyrm-minions to fight. Because that's the priority: fighting the Wyrm. The problems arise in <i>how </i>the Cult pursues the Wyrm and its minions. And so the Fenrir in Deepest of Wounds only become a problem once they come back and start looking for recruits and resources in order to go back out there to fight the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T14:18:23-08:00","id":1532061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531976-ten-tips-for-using-hauglosk-in-w5?p=1532060#post1532060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> sigh<br /> <br /> It says &quot;What do they want: The Cult of Fenris wants to fight the Wyrm, but its Garou see the presence of the Wyrm in all things.&quot; There's no &quot;especially other Garou&quot; here. It's pretty straightforward. Look, I like your version more but the thing is: It's not the official version that's in the corebook. The corebook disagrees with you on this. And Deepest of Wounds follows that. When the Fenrir-caern dies in the setup of that adventure, they start a raiding-party to venture out and go after the Wyrm. They don't turn on the other Garou in their vicinity, they go out and look for Wyrm-minions to fight. Because that's the priority: fighting the Wyrm. The problems arise in <i>how </i>the Cult pursues the Wyrm and its minions. And so the Fenrir in Deepest of Wounds only become a problem once they come back and start looking for recruits and resources in order to go back out there to fight the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I stand corrected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:20:28-08:00","id":1532111,"title":"","content":"I tend to think of the Cult of Fenris being at fault partly through unwavering fanaticism, but also because a majority of its members cultivate a \u201cVICTORY MEANS A GLORIOUS DEATH!\u201d (As in, \u2018If you\u2019re planning to come back from your next battle, you\u2019re doing something wrong not \u201cWin at all costs!\u201d) attitude.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re not fighting to Save the World, they\u2019re fighting for their own chance to die a Glorious Death and **** all optimists who dare claim there\u2019s any possibility for an honourable life without aiming for a Glorious Death sooner, rather than later.<br /> <br /> (One presumes that while this is the most common public attitude, those members who form the solid core of the Cult are more interested in making sure their colleague\u2019s Glorious Death is not wasted on some penny-ante operation).<br /> <br /> <br /> This is, to be clear, founded on my understanding that Hauglosk is fundamentally the Rage of Despair, not merely ungovernable fury.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}